{{~##
   A single self-contained Rust module: the enums, the constant sets, a struct and a
   table type per table, and the accessor that loads them together.

   References are resolved by index rather than by pointer, which is where this differs
   from the C++ and Go output. A record holding a reference to another record is a graph,
   and Rust will not let one own its neighbours; the alternative is lifetimes threaded
   through every generated type or a reference-counted cell around every row. Keeping the
   index and offering a lookup is simpler to read and costs the caller one call.

   Anything needing the model arrives already rendered from RustView.
##~}}
